; Regression test for issue #3243: xact fails to identify exact-match
;
; `xact bundt` drafted its transaction from "Lowes: flapper-seal and
; light-bulbs" although only "Nothing Bundt" matches the payee pattern
; "bundt".  draft_t::insert took whatever transaction the probabilistic
; payee lookup ranked highest, and consulted the payee pattern only when
; the lookup found nothing at all.  The lookup scored the Lowes payee 35,
; since b, u, n, d and t all occur in it, and "Nothing Bundt" below its
; threshold of 30.  Payees matching the pattern now outrank payees that
; merely resemble it, whatever their scores.

2026-06-25 * Lowes: flapper-seal and light-bulbs
    Expenses:Household:Home:Lowes          31.87 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

2026-06-26 ! Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Household:Food:Takeout:Nothing Bundt  5.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

test --now 2026/06/30 xact bundt
2026/06/30 Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Household:Food:Takeout:Nothing Bundt    5.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express
end test

; When no payee matches the pattern, the lookup still settles for the
; payee that most resembles it: the colon keeps "lowes flapper" from
; matching "Lowes: flapper-seal and light-bulbs".
test --now 2026/06/30 xact "lowes flapper"
2026/06/30 Lowes: flapper-seal and light-bulbs
    Expenses:Household:Home:Lowes          31.87 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express
end test
